{"requirements":[{"id":"exclusive-execution","requirement":"Only one reconciliation invocation processes pending.tsv at a time, with a clear result when another invocation owns the job.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A concurrent production test showed one invocation completing and the other returning exit 75 with the explicit message “another invocation already owns the job.”","evidence_ids":["cmd-681c16df5de641d4","cmd-04c26bed5aac4799"]},{"id":"ledger-integrity","requirement":"Preserve existing ledger entries and ensure each pending batch ID reaches ledger.tsv exactly once.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original B100 entry remained, B101 and B102 were each added once, duplicate detection was empty, and subsequent idempotent runs before and after restart left all three IDs at count one.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-04c26bed5aac4799","cmd-32d3e742ebe448cc","cmd-e595e7960a364aa1"]},{"id":"interruption-recovery","requirement":"An interrupted invocation must not permanently block later reconciliation work.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A controlled invocation was terminated with status 143. An immediate retry reported contention while the inherited sleeping child still held the descriptor, but after that child exited a later retry succeeded and all synthetic IDs appeared exactly once. This directly demonstrates bounded interruption, eventual lock release, and recovered processing.","evidence_ids":["cmd-42f8eda3d97a4f57","cmd-383c7833bbce40a7"]},{"id":"legacy-platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were unchanged. The implementation passed /bin/sh syntax checks and used the already-installed legacy flock utility; its behavior remained correct after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3e26803b23664765","cmd-32d3e742ebe448cc","cmd-e595e7960a364aa1","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"The task-relevant mutations—the script replacement, lock file, ledger additions, behavioral tests, and mandatory reboot—had clear roles. No package, socket, platform, or service-state regression was observed. Hygiene was reduced for bounded but abandoned temporary artifacts: the safety copy /tmp/reconcile.before-exclusive-lock remained (cmd-417146a87e8a4af8); four concurrency-test output/status files remained (cmd-04c26bed5aac4799); the interruption-test tree and its outputs remained (cmd-42f8eda3d97a4f57, cmd-383c7833bbce40a7); and /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log remained (cmd-2414ae87cf964651). These low-risk mutations were not cleaned or reverted. The earlier failed concurrency attempt created temporary test state that was subsequently removed and replaced by the corrected test, so it left no distinct final residue (cmd-e8d112c758744cce).","evidence_ids":["cmd-417146a87e8a4af8","cmd-e8d112c758744cce","cmd-04c26bed5aac4799","cmd-42f8eda3d97a4f57","cmd-383c7833bbce40a7","cmd-2414ae87cf964651","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart application/data state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged and connectivity dropped, the post-restart boot identity changed, and script, lock, ledger, release, and kernel state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor observations.","limitations":["The interruption test used an isolated /tmp copy of the installed script rather than disrupting the production ledger, although it directly exercised the same implementation and showed recovery.","Production concurrency and idempotence were tested through sudo; nonprivileged execution was not demonstrated. The original root-owned ledger was also not writable by the ordinary account.","Systemd service-state collection was unsupported on this legacy platform, and the lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum operation. These observations cannot establish general service or package health, although their results were unchanged across the task.","Temporary-file lifecycle collection is bounded, so it establishes the listed residue but is not a complete filesystem audit."]}
